  "text": "Share an ontology under Admin → IAM with the Ontology resource type. A grantee reads the published version, explores, asks, proposes changes and requests actions; editing, publishing and approving stay with the owner. A share can carry the same restrictions dashboard and semantic-model shares do: a row filter naming Type.property (or just a property, for every type that has it) and the values the grantee may see — a value like {{user.region}} becomes each viewer's own attribute; hidden properties, as Customer.email or email. Both are applied in every query the grantee runs — exploring, the object view, the graph, metrics, Ask and the agent tool. A hidden property reads as “hidden”, cannot be filtered, sorted, grouped or summed, and is left out of what AI is shown. A property marked restricted in the model is hidden from everyone but the owner. And because every query runs as the grantee, their own lakehouse grants and the tables' tag policies apply on top."
