  "text": "Export writes the model as the three Apache Ossie (incubating) documents — a semantic model (datasets, fields, relationships, metrics), an ontology (concepts and their relationships) and the mapping between them — so Snowflake, Databricks, dbt and other tools that read Ossie get the same definitions. What Ossie has no word for (a join-table link, a restricted property, rules, actions) travels in an AGENTSWARMS vendor extension, so exporting and importing again loses nothing. Other vendors' extensions are kept through a round trip. Import reads Ossie (a semantic model alone, or all three documents) or this app's JSON, and says what it could not carry. OWL (Turtle) is a one-way bridge for knowledge-graph tools."
